        "id": 10758,
        "name": "LevelUpLeo",
        "username": "LevelUpLeo",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/levelupleo/{size}/2394_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-07-17T02:30:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This scenario came up with Absolute Zero (Elemental Wraith) against Iron Legacy. Sub-Zero Atmosphere was in play, meaning Iron Legacy deals each hero target 3 melee damage at the START of the turn instead. Once, it was enough damage (due to modifiers) to Incapacitate Absolute Zero. We chose to have him take the damage first. We assumed this meant that, now that Sub-Zero Atmosphere was gone and Iron Legacy's attack returned to being at the end of a turn, his attack would stop. Was the the correct assumption, or would he still have attached the other hero targets?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:41:53.785Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
